<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Entitlements of the main executable (Contents/MacOS/logsquirl) and so of
      the app bundle, whose signature is the main executable's. Nothing else in
      the bundle is signed with an entitlements file: the Qt frameworks, the
      loose dylibs, the Qt plug-ins and the helper executables (logsquirl_grep,
      logsquirl_crashpad_handler, logsquirl_minidump_dump) get the hardened
      runtime alone, library validation included
      (.github/actions/mac-sign-notarize, #835).

      The hardened runtime's library validation only lets a process load
      libraries signed by Apple or by the same Team ID as the process. The main
      executable is the one process that loads Plugins, and a Plugin from the
      user plugin directory (ADR 0014) is signed by its author or not at all,
      so the main executable alone disables library validation. The helpers
      load nothing but the bundled frameworks, which carry the same signature,
      and the crashpad handler needs no entitlement of its own.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
